      {
        "narration": "A man jumped from a jet with $200,000 cash. November 24th, 1971, somewhere over southwest Washington, in the dark.",
        "visual_query": "boeing 727 night runway",
        "visual_fallback": "jet night"
      },
      {
        "narration": "He bought a ticket as Dan Cooper. Handed a note to a flight attendant, asked for four parachutes and ten thousand twenty-dollar bills.",
        "visual_query": "1970s airliner cabin interior",
        "visual_fallback": "airliner cabin"
      },
      {
        "narration": "Passengers released in Seattle. Then he lowered the rear airstair mid-flight and stepped out. The crew felt the tail pitch up at 8:13.",
        "visual_query": "pacific northwest forest night aerial",
        "visual_fallback": "dark forest"
      },
      {
        "narration": "How do you disappear carrying a sack of recorded serial numbers? For eight years, not one bill surfaced anywhere.",
        "visual_query": "columbia river washington shoreline",
        "visual_fallback": "wide river"
      },
      {
        "narration": "February 1980: an eight-year-old found three rotting packets on the Columbia River, six thousand dollars. The FBI shelved the case in 2016; its own agent had already concluded Cooper never survived the jump.",
        "visual_query": "columbia river sandy riverbank",
        "visual_fallback": "river sand"
      }
